  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 375 F. Set the pepper halves cut side up in a 9 by 13 inch baking dish.",
    "Heat 2 tbsp olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Cook the onion for 5 minutes, until soft.",
    "Add the garlic and zucchini. Cook for 4 minutes, until the zucchini starts to soften.",
    "Stir in the diced tomatoes with their juice, oregano, cumin, salt, and pepper. Simmer for 5 minutes, until thick.",
    "Remove the pan from the heat. Stir in the cooked rice, lemon juice, and parsley.",
    "Spoon the filling into the pepper halves, packing it in lightly. Pour the water into the bottom of the dish.",
    "Drizzle the peppers with the remaining 1 tbsp olive oil. Cover the dish tightly with foil.",
    "Bake for 25 minutes. Remove the foil and bake 10 to 15 minutes more, until the peppers are tender when pierced with a knife and the tops are lightly browned."
  ],
